speechtext:
Mr. JEAN-FRANQOIS POULIOT (Temis-couata): Mr. Speaker, by special leave of the house, if the house is unanimous in the matter, I wish to move:
Whereas the last meeting of the select standing committee on debates took place on June 17, 1931;
Whereas, before taking into consideration any further matter which might be referred to them by the house, a general and summary survey of the manner in which the past recommendations of this committee which have been approved by the house have been complied with during the last five years, shall be made;
Whereas a meeting of the said committee has been called for Thursday next, March 5;
That the said select standing committee on the debates shall take into consideration any matter within the scope of their jurisdiction and report to the house accordingly.
Right Hon. W. L. MACKENZIE KING
(Prime Minister): Mr. Speaker, I believe notice of motion will be required.
